-### Token Cards
+### Transformed Cards
 
-Temporary characters created by card effects. Tokens follow all normal character rules with these exceptions:
+The side a Hero becomes after using its once-per-game transformation (see *Hero Transformation*). When a Hero transforms, the Transformed card replaces the Hero in play, and its card type is **Transformed** rather than Hero. It uses the stats and abilities printed on the transformed side, keeps all damage from the base side, and grants access to the Hero's Ultimate ability.
 
-* **Removed from the game** — When a token would leave the battlefield for any reason (destroyed, exiled, bounced, returned to hand), it is removed from the game instead of going to the discard pile or hand.
-* **Cannot be targeted by discard pile effects** — Effects that reference cards in the discard pile cannot target or return tokens.
-* **Anti-loop clause** — If an effect would create an unbounded mandatory loop involving token creation, the loop stops after the third iteration.
-
-Tokens have stats, abilities, and traits as defined by the effect that created them. Unless otherwise specified, tokens have no resource cost.
+> **Note:** Tokens are not a card type. They are runtime artifacts created by other cards' effects — temporary characters that exist only in play. A token is removed from the game when it would leave the battlefield; it cannot be targeted by effects that reference cards in the discard pile; and if an effect would create an unbounded mandatory loop involving token creation, the loop stops after the third iteration.
 
